        {
          "_key": "research-edit-30-text",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "How a task comes back"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "research-edit-31",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "research-edit-31-text",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "I built the runner, launcher boundaries, and result collection. The agent works in a container with no network interface, a read-only root filesystem, dropped capabilities, and access to a task-scoped model gateway."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "research-edit-32",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "research-edit-32-text",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A trusted shadow Git directory collects the result without executing Git hooks from the agent-controlled checkout. A separate tool runs checks on the returned branch."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "research-edit-33",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "research-edit-33-text",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The trust boundary"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "research-edit-34",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "research-edit-34-text",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Docker launcher and model bridge are trusted components. gVisor is optional and changes the kernel boundary only when installed and selected. Public smoke tests do not establish resistance to every escape or replace an independent security assessment. Returned patches still require review."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
